Rule 4 (scalar lifting: either operand may be a scalar)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 5 (inputs must be safely broadcastable to avoid incompatible shapes error)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0) then true else (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 6 (inputs must have element types convertible to boolean; no string or dtype objects)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 0 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 7 (all dimension sizes are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : 0 ≤ shape(v_1, i)) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : 0 ≤ shape(v_2, j))
>>
Rule 9 (NumPy-style broadcasting compatibility across trailing axes)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : if (ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0) then true else shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 10 (equal-rank inputs must have identical shapes)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
